"@value": "Bicycle map (A bicycle map, also known as a bike map, is a specialized map designed to assist cyclists in navigating urban, suburban, or rural areas safely and efficiently. It typically highlights bike lanes, dedicated bike paths, shared roads, and other infrastructure that accommodates bicyclists. These maps may also include information on elevation changes, points of interest, bike racks, repair stations, and traffic conditions relevant to cyclists. Bicycle maps aim to provide cyclists with essential information to plan their routes, promote cycling as a mode of transportation, and enhance the overall biking experience by ensuring accessibility and safety)" } ] },  { "@id": "_:b49httpc0liddOtlocdOtgovauthoritiesgenreFormsgf2024026051", "@type": [ "http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#Source" ], "http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#citationStatus": [ { "@value": "found" } ], "http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#citationSource": [ { "@value": "Work cat.: Seattle (Wash.). Department of Transportation. 2022 Seattle bike map, 2022." } ], "http://www.loc.gov/mads/rdf/v1#citationNote": [ { "@language": "en",
